# kit:duplicate-corpus james-habits-app
#
# ⚠️ The brief handed to the writer of this file told it to add
# `# kit:not-a-real-app` as well. That directive is FALSE here — james-habits-app
# exists and ships — and it was removed by hand after the fact. Recorded rather
# than quietly deleted: I wrote the wrong instruction, the writer followed it
# correctly, and a corpus asserting something untrue about the world is the exact
# failure this project argues against. The honest exclusion is the line above.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TRIAL CORPUS — "James Habits App", written FORWARDS from the brief alone
#
# Written 2026-09-06, from docs/trials/habits-brief.md ONLY — no other file for
# this app was read (see the isolation note on claude-code-bot#92: "give a go
# building them from scratch based off my descriptions and comments"). The
# brief is James's opening ideation post plus his one follow-up comment on
# james-habits-app#1. Nothing else about that app informed this file.
#
# Every behaviour below is `source defined`, never `inferred` — there is no
# LLM inference step in this build, so an `inferred` line would be me
# hand-writing something and mislabelling it as a machine's work. Two anchors
# are used, both my own best-effort slugs of the brief's two headings (the
# brief has no per-bullet anchors, so behaviours drawing on the ideation list
# and the "keep it simple" follow-up share one anchor each):
#   #issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05   — the ideation post
#   #issue-1-comment-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05t120531z         — "keep simple... at
#                                                           the core just
#                                                           looking to track
#                                                           my habits"
#
# HONEST NOTE ON WHAT WAS HARD TO EXPRESS (see full findings in my report, this
# is the short version for anyone reading just this file):
#   - No verb asserts a control's ON/OFF state — `sees checkbox:X` proves the
#     control is present, not whether it is ticked. "Ticked it" and "reopened
#     already-ticked" end up asserting the identical fact.
#   - "Exercised - auto ticked by running" is a computed rule triggered by a
#     DIFFERENT noun's action. The notation has no way to state the RULE, only
#     a UI action plus a UI side-effect, same shape as trial-lend's TIMING gap.
#   - Every `when` in this notation is a user action. "Maybe some reminders?"
#     would be the app acting on its own (a clock, not a click) — a
#     structurally different kind of `when` that was never needed here because
#     it got cut, but is worth naming.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═══ Choosing what to track — "so i can taylor it to the exact ways that i
#     like to do things" means habits are user-defined, not a fixed list ═══

behaviour BEH-SETUP-1 "James opens habit setup to add something new to track"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05
  actor owner
  when opens page:ManageHabits
  when activates button:AddHabit
  then lands on page:NewHabit
  then sees field:HabitName

behaviour BEH-SETUP-2 "Saving a new habit adds it to today's list"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05
  actor owner
  when opens page:NewHabit
  when fills form:NewHabit with ?fields
  when activates button:SaveHabit
  then lands on page:Today
  then sees region:HabitList

behaviour BEH-SETUP-3 "A new habit needs nothing more than a name to be saved"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-comment-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05t120531z
  actor owner
  when opens page:NewHabit
  provides form:NewHabit.fields = HabitName


# ═══ The daily loop — "just a simple app to track my habits this year" ═══

behaviour BEH-TODAY-1 "Today's page lists everything currently being tracked"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05
  actor owner
  when opens page:Today
  then sees region:HabitList

behaviour BEH-TODAY-2 "Before any habit is added, today's page says there is nothing to track yet"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05
  actor owner
  given habits:None
  when opens page:Today
  then sees region:EmptyState

behaviour BEH-TODAY-3 "Ticking a habit marks it done for today"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05
  actor owner
  given habit:Pending
  when opens page:Today
  when activates checkbox:HabitDone
  then sees checkbox:HabitDone
  contract logging a habit is one tap, with no form or confirmation step in between

behaviour BEH-TODAY-4 "A habit ticked off earlier today still shows as done when the page is reopened"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05
  actor owner
  given habit:LoggedToday
  when opens page:Today
  then sees checkbox:HabitDone

behaviour BEH-TODAY-5 "Habits like sleeping hours or drinks drunk are logged as a number, not a tick"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05
  actor owner
  when opens page:Today
  when fills form:LogValue with ?fields
  when activates button:SaveValue
  then sees field:HabitValue

behaviour BEH-TODAY-6 "Each row in today's list shows the habit's own name"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05
  actor owner
  when opens page:Today
  then sees field:HabitName


# ═══ A habit that logs another — "Exercised - auto ticked by running" ═══

behaviour BEH-DERIVE-1 "Logging a run also marks Exercised as done, without ticking it directly"
  source defined docs/trials/habits-brief.md#issue-1-app-idea-opening-post-jemmy8oy-2026-07-05
  actor owner
  when opens page:Today
  when activates checkbox:Ran
  then shows badge:AutoTicked "Auto"


# ═══ The shapes the notation cannot state — recorded, not smuggled in ═══
#
# Each is a real requirement or near-requirement from the brief that a reader
# would expect this corpus to hold, and it cannot, without either inventing
# grammar or weakening the assertion below what the brief actually says:
#
#   BOOLEAN STATE   `sees checkbox:HabitDone` proves the control exists, not
#                    whether it is currently ticked. BEH-TODAY-3 ("just
#                    ticked") and BEH-TODAY-4 ("already ticked, reopened
#                    later") assert the IDENTICAL fact even though the human
#                    sentences describe different moments. For an app whose
#                    entire point is a done/not-done state, this is the
#                    biggest single gap found in this trial.
#
#   DERIVED RULES    "Exercised - auto ticked by running" is a rule relating
#                    two nouns (ticking Ran changes Exercised), not a fact
#                    about one screen. BEH-DERIVE-1 can only assert the
#                    visible SIDE EFFECT (a badge appears) after the trigger
#                    action; it cannot state the rule itself ("Exercised.done
#                    = Ran.done OR Exercised ticked directly"). Same shape as
#                    trial-lend's TIMING finding (a transition smuggled into a
#                    given-fixture or an after-the-fact badge, not stated as a
#                    rule a reviewer would read as a rule).
#
#   SYSTEM-INITIATED EVENTS   every `when` in this notation is something an
#                    actor does. "Maybe some reminders?" and any notification,
#                    daily reset, or scheduled rollover the brief gestures at
#                    would need a `when` with no actor behind it — a clock,
#                    not a click. Not attempted here (reminders were cut as
#                    non-core — see report), but it is a different SHAPE of
#                    when, not just a missing noun.
#
#   QUANTITATIVE COMPARISON   "Goals? Progress bars? On track etc" (cut as
#                    non-core) would need the app to assert an arithmetic
#                    relationship ("5 of 7 days this week" being "on track").
#                    The notation could only show the rendered literal text of
#                    the result (`shows label:X "5/7"`), never the comparison
#                    that produced it — not attempted, since the feature
#                    itself was cut, but the same shape as DERIVED RULES above.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
